  "system_findings": [
    "Transformers, switchgear, copper, power semiconductors, digital controls, and skilled electrical labor are shared dependencies across generators, transmission, data centers, chargers, buildings, and factories; sector forecasts therefore compete for the same capacity.",
    "A generation technology's module or turbine factory is only one layer. Interconnection equipment, civil works, transport, fuel or critical-material inputs, workforce, and end-of-life handling can become the binding constraint.",
    "Announced factories and funded projects must be tracked separately from operating qualified capacity and actual output.",
    "Fuel supply chains remain operational constraints for gas, coal, nuclear, and bioenergy even after a power plant is built.",
    "Demand flexibility can reduce peak infrastructure requirements but does not erase annual energy, local reliability, or minimum-service obligations."
  ]
}
